{
 "_about": "Stackups for the measurement coupons (validation/test_board/README.md). Copper and dielectric thicknesses in mm, top (L1) to bottom. 'planes' are the copper layers (0 = L1) that carry the GND reference planes on the coupons. Every value has a source; values marked 'assumption' or 'estimate' are not published by the manufacturer and are to be replaced by extracted values (line and cavity coupons) or by the manufacturer's stackup report. 'pdn.pwr' is the plane layer that carries the PWR islands of the PDN coupons.",
 "_fetched": "2026-10-22",
 "sources": {
  "jlc_api": {
   "what": "Layer list and thicknesses of JLCPCB's impedance templates (raw JSON of JLC's impedance-template web API), captured by gsuberland/jlcpcb_autogenerated_stackups, commit 9c8b685 (2025-05-20). The raw JSON is JLCPCB's data; the template names are the ones selected in JLC's order form.",
   "url": "https://github.com/gsuberland/jlcpcb_autogenerated_stackups/tree/main/raw_json",
   "note": "JLC's own impedance pages (jlcpcb.com/impedance, jlcpcb.com/pcb-impedance-calculator) could not be fetched from this workspace; check the template still exists in the order form before ordering."
  },
  "jlc_capabilities": {
   "what": "JLCPCB PCB capabilities page: dielectric constants '7628 prepreg 4.4, 3313 prepreg 4.1, 2116 prepreg 4.16' (text partly run together on the page), solder mask 3.8, impedance tolerance +/-10 % (+/-5 % on request), FR-4 Grade A laminate (Nan Ya, KB, Shengyi), board thickness tolerance +/-10 %, track width tolerance +/-20 %.",
   "url": "https://jlcpcb.com/capabilities/pcb-capabilities"
  },
  "jlc_impedance_guide": {
   "what": "JLCPCB 'User Guide to the JLCPCB Impedance Calculator': laminate Nan Ya NP-155F for 4-8 layers; solder mask 1.2 mil on laminate, 0.6 mil on copper, 1.2 mil between traces, er 3.8; external 1 oz copper calculated as 1.6 mil, internal 0.5 oz as 0.6 mil (15.2 um); trace top width = base width - 0.7 mil.",
   "url": "https://jlcpcb.com/help/article/user-guide-to-the-jlcpcb-impedance-calculator"
  },
  "jitx_jlc_materials": {
   "what": "JITX library jitxlib.jlcpcb.materials: FR-4 core Dk 4.6 'From Impedance Control Specifications from JLC-PCB' (@1 GHz), prepregs 7628 4.4 / 2116 4.16 / 1080 3.91 (a secondary source, used for the core).",
   "url": "https://docs.jitx.com/en/latest/_modules/jitxlib/jlcpcb/materials.html"
  },
  "np155f_by_core": {
   "what": "NP-155F core Dk by core thickness as tabulated in the generator script of gsuberland/jlcpcb_autogenerated_stackups (from the NP-155F datasheet): 0.40 mm 4.36, 0.55 mm 4.41, >0.70 mm 4.43; tan d 0.02. An alternative to the 4.6 of JITX; the coupons measure it (G cavity, stripline lines).",
   "url": "https://github.com/gsuberland/jlcpcb_autogenerated_stackups/blob/main/generate_stackups.linq"
  },
  "aisler_community": {
   "what": "Aisler community posts by Aisler staff: 4-layer 1.6 mm uses 'different stock depending on current availability for the core and prepreg', which 'can lead to variations in thickness and impedance'; a specific stackup only through the sales team (posts of 2026-02-03 / 2026-03-25). Older posts (2023-10): Panasonic prepreg 1080 type R-1551(W), 18 um base foil plated to >= 35 um on the outer layers.",
   "url": "https://community.aisler.net/t/4-layers-1-6mm-70-m-stackup/5523",
   "url2": "https://community.aisler.net/t/altium-4-layers-stackup/3168"
  }
